{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>And Pharaoh drew near.</b> That is, he brought himself near. And in the Midrash: 'he brought the punishment upon himself,' because he sacrificed and offered incense to Ba'al Zephon, for he saw them encamped before Ba'al Zephon and thought that its power had trapped them in the wilderness so that they could not escape. Another interpretation: 'And Pharaoh drew near' — he brought Israel near, to return to their Father in heaven. This is what the Sages, of blessed memory, said: the Holy One, blessed be He, sets over them a king like the wicked Haman and thereby returns them to the good. And this is what it says — immediately:" "<b>And the children of Israel lifted up their eyes, etc., and the children of Israel cried out to YHWH.</b> They took up the craft of their fathers: of Abraham it is written (Genesis 19): ״וישכם אברהם בבקר אל המקום״; of Isaac it is written (Genesis 24): ״ויצא יצחק לשוח בשדה״; of Jacob (ibid. 28): ״ויפגע במקום״. And on this Israel was likened to a worm, as it says (Isaiah 41): ״אל תיראי תולעת יעקב״ — just as this worm strikes the cedars only with its mouth, and it is soft yet strikes something hard, so Israel has nothing but prayer, since the idolatrous nations were likened to cedars, as it says (Ezekiel 31): ״הנה אשור ארז בלבנון״, and it is written (Psalms 29): ״וישבר ה׳ את ארזי הלבנון״. And Israel prevails by means of Torah and prayer, as it says (Deuteronomy 4): ״ובקשת משם את ה׳ אלהיך ומצאת״, and it is written (Psalms 20): ״אלה ברכב ואלה בסוסים ואנחנו בשם ה׳ אלהינו נזכיר״." "<b>And behold, Egypt is journeying after them.</b> It should have said נוסעים (journeying, plural), and by way of the plain sense (peshat) it teaches that the Egyptians were of one heart, as one man, in coming against Israel." "<b>And by way of</b> the Midrash: 'and behold, Egypt is journeying after them' — they saw the prince of Egypt journeying from heaven to help Egypt, and this was עזא, and so I have found in the Midrash: 'ויושע עזא — the prince of Egypt.'"], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:58:58.650728267Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}